{
  "_README": [
    "PRICES IN THIS FILE ARE ESTIMATES, NOT REAL ADVERTISED PRICES.",
    "They were written by hand as plausible Auckland supermarket prices so the",
    "costing engine has something to work on. Nothing in this project fetches",
    "live prices. Treat every number here as a placeholder until you replace it",
    "with what you actually paid, or wire up a real source.",
    "",
    "The 'specials' below are invented too. They exist to prove the",
    "cheaper-elsewhere report works, not to tell you what is on special.",
    "",
    "To maintain this by hand: the easiest habit is to correct an item's price",
    "the next time you buy it. Prices you have checked yourself can be marked",
    "with \"checked\": \"YYYY-MM-DD\" and the page will trust them visibly more.",
    "",
    "unit:          what the price is quoted per - 'g', 'ml' or 'each'",
    "per / price:   price dollars for that many units (e.g. per 1000 g)",
    "g_per_unit:    typical weight of one, so '2 onions' can be costed",
    "g_per_ml:      density, so 'cups of flour' can be costed by weight",
    "staple:        assumed already in the cupboard",
    "free_allowance: how much of a staple is free before the excess is charged",
    "where you shop:  lives in config.json (primary_store), not here -- this file holds a price per chain and the config picks which one is yours"
